Feature: Conversion of Spark.SQL to PySpark

  Background:
    Given the environment configuration is set as per requirements
    And dependencies such as Constants and ReusableFunctions are available

  Scenario Outline: Successful conversion of SQL code to PySpark
    Given the raw data is loaded from <sourceTable> into a DataFrame
    When the transformation logic is applied to the DataFrames
    Then the resulting DataFrame should be written to <targetTable> in Unity Catalog
    And the partitionOverwriteMode should be set to "dynamic"
    And the partition key should be "<partitionKey>"
    And column formats and types should be respected

    Examples:
      | sourceTable                        | targetTable                 | partitionKey |
      | raw_unity_catalog.dw_ap_sla_aging_invoice_ca | purgo_playground.f_supplier_invoice | invoice_id   |
      | raw_unity_catalog.dw_ap_sla_expense_dist_cf | purgo_playground.supplier_invoice   | gl_code_combination_id |

  Scenario: Handling missing dependencies with error
    Given dependencies like Constants and ReusableFunctions are not available
    When the Spark job is executed
    Then an error message "Required dependencies missing: Constants, ReusableFunctions" should be logged

  Scenario: Error in table resolution
    Given an incorrect source table name "raw_unity_catalog.invalid_table"
    When the job tries to access the invalid table
    Then an error message "Table raw_unity_catalog.invalid_table does not exist" should be thrown

  Scenario Outline: Validation of data formats and casting
    Given data is read from <sourceTable> with expected formats
    When the data is cast and transformed
    Then ensure all dates are in "yyyyMMdd" format
    And ensure all amounts are cast to double
    And strings should not exceed expected lengths

    Examples:
      | sourceTable                          |
      | raw_unity_catalog.dw_ap_sla_aging_invoice_ca |
      | raw_unity_catalog.dw_ap_sla_expense_dist_cf |

  Scenario: Validation of partition overwrite mode setting
    Given the Spark config for sources.partitionOverwriteMode
    When setting is checked
    Then ensure it is "dynamic"

  Scenario: Handling missing configuration values
    Given a missing config for dbutils.widgets
    When attempting to retrieve configuration
    Then an error message "Configuration value for <configKey> is missing" should be thrown

  Scenario Outline: Data-driven tests for invoice transformation
    Given selected columns from <sourceTable>
    When transformation logic is applied
    Then validate the presence of transformed data in output table
    And transformed values should match expected results

    Examples:
      | sourceTable | expectedOutput             |
      | raw_unity_catalog.dw_ap_sla_aging_invoice_ca | purgo_playground.supplier_invoice |

